Here is a complete, copy-pasteable script using HTML and CSS. 

### The Concept
To achieve a "Gradient Border" effect without external images, we use a clever overlay technique:
1.  **The Core Text:** This is the white text you actually read.
2.  **The Overlay (Pseudo-element):** We place a duplicate of the text slightly *larger* behind the core text. We apply a rainbow gradient to this larger text using `background-clip: text`. Because it is larger, it peeks out from the edges of the white core text, creating the illusion of a glowing rainbow border.
3.  **The Glow:** We add CSS `text-shadow` to intensify the lighting effect.

### The Code

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Rainbow Glowing Text</title>
    <style>
        /* 1. Page Setup: Dark background is essential for glowing effects */
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            height: 100vh;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            background-color: #0f0c29; /* Deep space blue/black */
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        /* 2. Container Card */
        .container {
            position: relative;
            z-index: 10;
        }

        /* 3. The Wrapper (Shared styling for the real text and the ghost text) */
        .glow-wrapper {
            display: inline-block;
            font-weight: 900;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 5px;
            /* We disable selection to keep it looking clean */
            user-select: none; 
        }

        /* ----------------------------------------------------
           THE RAINBOW BORDER LAYER (The "Ghost")
           ---------------------------------------------------- */
        .glow-wrapper::before {
            content: attr(data-text); /* Pulls text from data attribute */

            position: absolute;
            top: 0;
            left: 0;

            /* Make it slightly larger to create the border thickness */
            font-size: 150%; 

            /* This creates the rainbow background */
            background: linear-gradient(
                135deg, 
                #ff0000, 
                #ff7f00, 
                #ffff00, 
                #00ff00, 
                #0000ff, 
                #4b0082, 
                #9400d3
            );

            /* Clipping: Only show the gradient on the text shape */
            -webkit-background-clip: text;
            background-clip: text;

            /* Turn the text transparent so it doesn't block the white text underneath */
            color: transparent;

            /* Blur it slightly to make the edge softer */
            filter: blur(2px);

            /* Center alignment fix */
            line-height: 1em;
            pointer-events: none; /* Allow clicking through */

            /* ANIMATION: Moves the gradient across the text */
            animation: animateGradient 6s linear infinite;
        }

        /* ----------------------------------------------------
           THE CORE WHITE TEXT (The Readable Part)
           ---------------------------------------------------- */
        .real-text {
            position: relative;
            z-index: 2;

            /* Bright white center */
            color: #ffffff; 

            /* The Intense Glow Effect */
            text-shadow: 
                0 0 5px  rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8),
                0 0 10px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6),
                0 0 20px rgba(0, 255, 255, 0.4), /* Cyan tint for sci-fi look */
                0 0 30px rgba(138, 43, 226, 0.3),/* Purple tint */

                /* Adding the colored glow matching the rainbow border */
                0 0 10px rgba(255, 0, 0, 0.2),
                0 0 20px rgba(0, 0, 255, 0.2);

            font-size: 3rem;
            line-height: 1em;
        }

        /* ----------------------------------------------------
           KEYFRAMES FOR ANIMATION
           ---------------------------------------------------- */
        @keyframes animateGradient {
            0% {
                background-position: 0% 50%;
            }
            50% {
                background-position: 100% 50%;
            }
            100% {
                background-position: 0% 50%;
            }
        }

        /* Responsiveness for mobile screens */
        @media (max-width: 600px) {
            .real-text {
                font-size: 1.5rem;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="container">
        <!-- 
          IMPORTANT: We use a data-text attribute. 
          This allows the ::before pseudo-element to pull the text automatically
          without writing it twice in the HTML.
        -->
        <span class="glow-wrapper" data-text="NEON GLOW">NEON GLOW</span>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
