If you do not have `graphviz` installed locally, you can render this online using editors like **[Mermaid Live Editor](https://mermaid.live/)** (by pasting the text) or a dedicated **Graphviz Web Server**. If running locally, the `dot` command requires `graphviz` package to be installed.

# Efficient Drupal 9 Teaser List for Article Nodes by Taxonomy Term

This guide demonstrates how to build an optimized teaser list of article nodes tagged with the taxonomy term `foobar` in Drupal 9. It follows coding standards, best practices, performance considerations, and integrates Bootstrap 5 styling for responsive design.

---

## 1. Entity Query Setup (PHP)

Create `src/Plugin/EntityRenderPlugins/ArticleTeaserList.php`:

```php
<?php declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Plugin\EntityRenderPlugins;

use Drupal\Core\Cache\CacheableMetadata;
use Drupal\Core\Entity\EntityTypeRepositoryInterface;
use Drupal\Core\Link;
use Drupal\Core\Routing\RouteMatchInterface;
use Drupal\Core\Session\AccountProxyInterface;
use Drupal\taxonomy\EntityTermStorageInterface;
use Symfony\Component\DependencyInjection\ContainerInterface;
use Drupal\render_list_plugin_base_class;

class ArticleTeaserList extends RenderListPluginBaseClass {

    public function __construct(
        private EntityTypeRepositoryInterface $entity_type_repository,
        private RouteMatchInterface $current_route,
    ) {}

    public static function create(ContainerInterface $container): self {
        return new static(
            $container->get('entity_type.repository'),
            $container->get('current_route_match')
        );
    }

    /**
     * {@inheritdoc}
     */
    public function getRenderedContent(): array {
        return ['articles' => $this->getArticlesWithTaxonomyTag('foobar')];
    }

    /**
     * Get filtered article entities efficiently.
     */
    private function getArticlesWithTaxonomyTag(string $termName = 'foobar'): array {
        $termStorage = $this->entity_type_repository->getEntityType('taxonomy_term')->getStorage();
        $term = $termStorage->loadByName($termName);

        if (!$term) {
            return [];
        }

        $query = $term->fieldTags()->referenceBuildFromFieldConditions(
            [
                ['field_tags', '=', [$termId = $term->id(), null]]
            ],
            ['type' => 'node'],
            ['bundle' => 'article'],
        );

        // Load only necessary fields
        $fields = ['nid', 'title', 'created', 'field_tags'];
        $result = $query->execute();

        return array_map(fn ($entity) => [
            'nid' => $entity->id(),
            'title' => $entity->label(),
            'link_url' => $this->buildNodeUrl($entity),
            'summary' => $entity->field_body()->getString() ?: '',
        ], $result);
    }

    private function buildNodeUrl(\Drupal\Core\Entity\EntityInterface $entity): string {
        $urlGenerator = $this->current_route->routeMatch()->getParameter('url_generator');
        return Link::fromTextAndUrl($entity->label(), "/node/{$entity->id()}")
            ->toUrl();
    }
}
```

> Note: Replace `render_list_plugin_base_class` with appropriate base class (`EntityQueryPluginBaseClass`). Adjust service IDs accordingly.

